  "interpretation": "The source proves the current single-registry bridge rejects a second callback registration while active and the current UVM implementation binds an ioctl fd to one file-operations identity. It does not prove that separately renamed UVM modules or a complete user-space router are impossible. The shared system-memory mapping is selected only as the smallest first experiment, not as a proven API capability. The public UVM prototypes expose no typed Linux-page/DMA/SG/dma-buf import surface. MemoryAllocSys plus DupAllocation is a candidate system-memory mapping path, but cross-provider RM semantics are undocumented and hidden behind proprietary rm_gpu_ops. PMA returns GPU physical addresses owned by a per-device PMA object; SetPageDirectory programs one GPU VA space's page-table root. Neither is a generic host-page import. DMA, coherence, semaphore correctness and hardware behavior remain unvalidated.",
  "observed_at_utc": "2026-10-23T21:01:37.711514+00:00",
